.\" Man page for archinstallsuper(8)
.\" Generated for ArchinstallSuper v0.11.0
.TH ARCHINSTALLSUPER 8 "2026-11-26" "ArchinstallSuper 0.11.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
archinstallsuper \- standalone UEFI installer for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B archinstallsuper
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B archinstallsuper \fI--config\fR \fIFILE\fR \fI--auto\fR
.br
.B archinstallsuper \fI--example-config\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ArchinstallSuper
is a standalone, full-screen UEFI installer for Arch Linux. It does not
depend on or use the official \fBarchinstall\fR package. Instead it uses
standard Arch tooling (\fBpacstrap\fR, \fBpacman\fR, \fBsgdisk\fR,
\fBmkfs\fR, \fBsystemd-boot\fR, \fBmkinitcpio\fR, \fBcryptsetup\fR) to
perform a safe, confirmed installation.

The installer supports three run modes:

.TP
\fBInteractive\fR (default)
A modern full-screen TUI (Python/curses) guides the user through profile,
kernel, filesystem, disk, system settings, encryption and final confirmation.
\fBdialog\fR and plain-text backends are available as fallbacks.

.TP
\fBUnattended\fR (\fB--config\fR \fIFILE\fR \fB--auto\fR)
Reads settings from a configuration file and performs the installation without
any interactive prompts. Suitable for automated deployments and CI.

.TP
\fBCheck-only\fR (\fB--check\fR)
Validates the live environment (UEFI, x86_64, network, required commands)
without modifying any disk.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--check\fR
Run preflight validation only (UEFI, live ISO, network). Exit 0 on success.

.TP
\fB--dry-run\fR
Collect settings, show the plan and validate packages, but do not modify any
disk.

.TP
\fB--plain\fR
Do not use the full-screen TUI; run in plain text mode.

.TP
\fB--debug\fR
Enable verbose debug output in the log.

.TP
\fB--log\fR \fIFILE\fR
Write the installation log to \fIFILE\fR instead of the default
\fI/var/log/archinstallsuper.log\fR.

.TP
\fB--config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Use \fIFILE\fR as an unattended installation configuration file. Implies
loading values as defaults in interactive mode.

.TP
\fB--auto\fR
Run unattended installation. Requires \fB--config\fR. No UI is shown.

.TP
\fB--example-config\fR
Print a sample configuration file to stdout and exit.

.TP
\fB--version\fR
Print version and exit.

.TP
\fB--help\fR,\ \fB-h\fR
Show usage information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
An unattended configuration file uses INI-like syntax:

.TP
\fB[system]\fR
hostname, username, timezone, locale, keymap, root_policy (password|locked), zram (true|false)

.TP
\fB[install]\fR
mode (minimal|basic|full|custom), desktop (gnome|kde|xfce|cinnamon), kernel (linux|linux-lts|linux-zen|linux-hardened), filesystem (ext4|btrfs|xfs), encryption (true|false), luks_password, root_password, user_password, efi_size_mib

.TP
\fB[disk]\fR
device (e.g. /dev/nvme0n1), efi_size_mib

.TP
\fB[packages]\fR
extra (space-separated package names)

.TP
\fB[network]\fR
wifi_ssid, wifi_password

Passwords are read from the file but never written to the log.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/var/log/archinstallsuper.log\fR
Installation log (mode 0600).
.TP
\fI/run/archinstallsuper/installer.lock\fR
Single-instance lock to prevent concurrent runs.
.SH SECURITY
.PP
The installer never writes passwords to the log or command line.
\fBchpasswd\fR receives passwords through a pipe; \fBcryptsetup\fR reads the
passphrase from stdin via \fB--key-file -\fR. Password variables are unset
immediately after use.
.PP
Only x86_64 UEFI is supported; Legacy BIOS/CSM and MBR are not. A normal run
erases the selected disk completely after two explicit confirmations
(\fBERASE <disk>\fR and \fBINSTALL\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive installation:
.B archinstallsuper
.TP
Unattended installation from a config file:
.B archinstallsuper --config myconfig.conf --auto
.TP
Check the live environment before installing:
.B archinstallsuper --check
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install (1),\ pacstrap (8),\ systemd-boot (1),\ cryptsetup (8)
